# Allowlist, not a denylist — same reasoning as claude/.gitignore.
#
# Ammonite fills ~/.ammonite with history, cache/, .scala-build/ and a
# per-JDK rt-*.jar that runs to tens of megabytes each. install.sh creates
# ~/.ammonite before stowing so stow folds into it and that state stays in
# $HOME, but this is the second line of defence: if the fold guard is ever
# lost, the whole directory becomes a symlink into this package and the next
# REPL start commits hundreds of megabytes of JARs. Naming the runtime paths
# one by one would go stale, so ignore everything and re-include only the
# three tracked scripts.
#
# A directory has to be un-ignored before a file inside it can be, hence the
# separate `!.ammonite/` line — git never descends into an excluded
# directory. See https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore

*
!.gitignore
!.stow-local-ignore
!.ammonite/
!.ammonite/predef.sc
!.ammonite/helper.sc
!.ammonite/import.sc
